Date: Thu, 02 Sep 93 09:04:25 -0500
From: "Patrick M. Fitzgerald" <pmfitzge@fitz.b30.ingr.com>
Subject: Meta: I have a problem using the list software with MH 

In message #93-9-32 
davisd@nimitz.ee.washington.edu writes:
> 
> I use MH through emacs. MH automatically inserts a blank line between
> the headers and the text.

I don't think MH is your problem.  You probably need to check with
extropians-request to make sure the list software is correctly
recognizing your address (otherwise, it won't accept commands from
you).  I had that problem for a couple weeks, until habs fixed me up.

The only problem I had with MH is that the list software did not
recognize the default MH In-reply-to: header; thus, I could not reply
to a message and, for example, put "::exclude thread" at the top.  But
since MH lets you customize your headers, I just changed the replcomps
file from

	%<(nodate{date})%{date}%|%(pretty{date})%>."%<{message-id}
	             %{message-id}%>\n%>\

to

	%<{date}In-reply-to: %{message-id}\n%>\

and now everything works fine.
