>news to me.  Are potential and kinetic energy just a fiction that physicists
>use to keep the books square?

I think you'll find that the real problem is that you're trying to mix relativity
and newtonian physics. I'm not certain, but I strongly suspect that if you used 
general relativity instead of newtonian gravity then this whole situation would 
disappear.

